WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.580
So the more we look at polling, the more we
might think that Joe Biden and Kamala Harris

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.379
have this election in the bag.

00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:12.140
But consider for a moment that even if the
polls are both perfectly accurate and don't

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.330
change between now and Election Day, what
about voter suppression?

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:23.570
Because the Supreme Court just showed us that
at least three of the justices are more than

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.470
willing to throw out absentee ballots.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:30.730
And that is not priced into the polls in any
way.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:37.700
The Supreme Court has reinstated South Carolina's
witness signature requirement for absentee

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.700
ballots.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.289
They did this earlier this week.

00:00:40.289 --> 00:00:46.620
That alone is a decision that could decide
whether Lindsey Graham is reelected as a Republican

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.530
incumbent in South Carolina or whether Challenger
date.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:55.810
Jamie Harrison from the Democratic Party removes
incumbent Lindsey Graham.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.550
That is what the stakes are here.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:03.750
And it means that South Carolinians, including
those infected with Corona virus, will once

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:08.110
again need witnesses to sign their ballot
envelopes.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.579
So think that through for a second.

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:13.350
You have corona virus or you want to avoid
getting it.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.960
You have it and want to avoid spreading it.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.250
Or you shouldn't go out or you want to avoid
getting it from someone else.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.200
You just want to be as safe as possible.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.850
You request an absentee ballot.

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:22.850
Beautiful.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.149
You get the absentee ballot.

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:25.149
Perfect.

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:27.750
You fill out the absentee ballot correctly.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.750
Lovely.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.380
But before you send it in.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:35.479
You need to find a witness to sign the envelope
for you that says it's really you voting.

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:36.759
It's really you sending this thing.

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:42.290
And it's pointless because that signature
could, of course, before it risks spreading

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.500
the virus.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.610
And it will almost certainly lead to the nullification
of ballots.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.980
But that's not the worst of it.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:58.530
It's even worse potentially because Justices
Clarence Thomas, Samuel Alito and Neil Gorsuch

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:04.149
would have been willing not just to say that
these ballots going forward must have a witness

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:11.020
signature, but Thomas, Alito and Gorsuch actually
were ready to say this rule should be applied

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.510
retroactively.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.660
So I really need people to understand this.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:22.099
Clarence Thomas, Samuel Alito and Neil Gorsuch
would be onboard with saying ballots already

00:02:22.099 --> 00:02:27.950
received by South Carolina election officials
before this decision was made about witness

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.480
signatures.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:34.370
Those ballots should be thrown out, even though
at the time that folks sent their ballots

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:39.230
in this witness signature rule was not yet
the rule.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:42.510
It is outrageous and extreme.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:49.810
And what it signals to me is that if indeed
they get Amy Kelt CONI Barat confirmed to

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:56.750
the Supreme Court and if indeed this entire
presidential election starts to extend into

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:03.110
November and starts to involve courts, there
are already three.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.400
Amy CONI Barrett could be a fourth.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.190
And then you then it's just a question mark.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:08.230
What will John Roberts do?

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.620
What will others do?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:14.650
They are willing to actually interfere in
ways that are material.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.250
These are not theoretical things.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.840
These are not things that might have an impact.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.790
But two or four years from now, this is right
now.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:27.370
And had they gotten this rule passed, the
retroactive requirement for witness signatures,

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.879
that would have led to I don't even know how
many ballots being thrown out that could have

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:37.180
led to Lindsey Graham winning, even if Jamie
Harrison would otherwise have won.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.200
I mean, we don't know.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.390
That's going to be a tight race and it's an
uphill battle for Jamie Harrison.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:46.299
But the point here is the Trump administration
is going to use this to their advantage in

00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:47.640
any way that they can.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.950
The Trump campaign has an army of lawyers
ready to do anything they can in any state.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.709
They can do it to see what they can get away
with.

00:03:56.709 --> 00:03:59.420
Biden has a team of lawyers.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.110
But are they ready?

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:05.890
As I've said before, it's much more difficult
to play defense because you need to anticipate

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.610
every strategy that Trump can use.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:12.680
Trump might have 10 different strategies lawyers
will use and Biden's lawyers might anticipate

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.680
nine of them.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.910
And it could be that tenth one that actually
gets you in the end.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:20.360
So they really need to be prepared because
Trump wants to win.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:27.440
Trump, at this point can only win by preventing
people from voting, by dissuading people from

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.550
voting, by having people's votes not counted.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:34.820
And Republicans have repeatedly said in public
that this is the plan.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:39.440
No one should be surprised now that they are
actually making the plan a reality.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:45.440
And if it comes to just a couple of states,
which it might, and the Supreme Court invalidates

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.930
hundreds of thousands of votes, more than
that, will there be a revolt?

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.700
I actually think, you know, I don't have.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:58.470
I have what I think is a realistic assessment
that most people cannot.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:03.550
Or to miss the next day of work and most people
are not going to mass rally and go protest

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:07.160
because they have people to feed and money
to make and bills to pay.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.730
And I understand that.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:15.390
But I actually think that if it appears as
though a Supreme Court with multiple justices

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:21.190
on it selected by Donald Trump in starts invalidating
votes and potentially flips the election to

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:25.290
Trump, I do believe there will be complete
actual chaos in the streets.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.550
I believe we will see mass rallies.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.960
I do believe that.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.790
And I rarely am of that mindset.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:31.690
Let me know what you think

